# Rank 1069 / CVE-2026-42520: the Jenkins credentials-binding plugin wrote a
# file credential to the name the credential itself carries, so a name with
# traversal in it escaped the temporary directory the build was given
# (CWE-22, SECURITY-3672). FileBinding and ZipFileBinding both held
#
#   FilePath secret = dir.child(credentials.getFileName());
#
# and the fix takes the base name first, `new File(credentials.getFileName()).getName()`.
# Pool commit 3f6decef43 is the real fix (COMMIT_OK by content, two source files
# and a regression test; the metadata check reported COMMIT_NONE because the
# advisory names the Jenkins security bulletin rather than a commit).
# No pool correction.
#
# ATTENTION, and the sink gap here is a symptom of something larger. Nothing is
# labelled in either file: FilePath.child is Jenkins' documented way to resolve a
# path under a directory and no binding names it, so there is no sink, and the
# credential's own file name is not a source either.
#
# The binding that would say it cannot be written the way the others are. A
# binding matches callee.path or callee.method, and the receiver in the graph is
# the variable, `dir.child`, not its type, so the only general form is
# `callee.method == "child"`, which names every child accessor in every tree API.
# The construct that exists for exactly this, a `requires { dependency(...) }`
# gate, is inert here: the SCA manifest table in internal/extract/sca/discover.go
# reads requirements.txt, setup.py, setup.cfg, package.json, .npmrc,
# composer.lock, go.mod and cargo.lock, and no Maven or Gradle file, so a Java
# project never has a known dependency. Measured with a pom.xml declaring
# ant:ant beside a call to the method the ant:ant-gated binding matches: the
# label does not appear. Every dependency-gated binding for the JVM languages
# and for C# is unreachable the same way -- 1421 for java, 1663 kotlin, 1498
# scala, 1388 groovy, 409 csharp -- which is 6379 bindings that no scan can
# fire. Recorded in ENGINE-GAPS.md.
#
# The two snippets differ only in whether the name is taken as a base name.
#
# verify_current_expected: attention-engine-gap

test "rank1069: the credential's own file name becomes the path"
  lang java
  file src/main/java/org/jenkinsci/plugins/credentialsbinding/impl/FileBinding.java
  reject VYQL-PATH-001
  code
  ```
  package org.jenkinsci.plugins.credentialsbinding.impl;

  import hudson.FilePath;
  import java.io.IOException;
  import java.io.InputStream;

  public class FileBinding extends AbstractOnDiskBinding<FileCredentials> {

      @Override
      protected FilePath write(FileCredentials credentials, FilePath dir) throws IOException, InterruptedException {
          FilePath secret = dir.child(credentials.getFileName());
          try (InputStream in = credentials.getContent()) {
              secret.copyFrom(in);
          }
          secret.chmod(0400);
          return secret;
      }
  }
  ```

test "rank1069: the same write taking the base name first"
  lang java
  file src/main/java/org/jenkinsci/plugins/credentialsbinding/impl/FileBinding.java
  reject VYQL-PATH-001
  code
  ```
  package org.jenkinsci.plugins.credentialsbinding.impl;

  import hudson.FilePath;
  import java.io.File;
  import java.io.IOException;
  import java.io.InputStream;

  public class FileBinding extends AbstractOnDiskBinding<FileCredentials> {

      @Override
      protected FilePath write(FileCredentials credentials, FilePath dir) throws IOException, InterruptedException {
          String baseName = new File(credentials.getFileName()).getName();

          FilePath secret = dir.child(baseName);
          try (InputStream in = credentials.getContent()) {
              secret.copyFrom(in);
          }
          secret.chmod(0400);
          return secret;
      }
  }
  ```
